  "title": "Chapter 9.1 — Properties of Radicals",
  "id": "chapter-9-1-flashcards",
  "cards": [
    {
      "back": "$$ \\sqrt{ab} = \\sqrt{a} \\cdot \\sqrt{b} $$ for $a, b \\ge 0$. Example: $\\sqrt{9 \\cdot 5} = 3\\sqrt{5}$.",
      "front": "State the [[kw:Product Property of Square Roots]]."
    },
    {
      "front": "State the [[kw:Quotient Property of Square Roots]].",
      "back": "$$ \\sqrt{\\frac{a}{b}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{a}}{\\sqrt{b}} $$ for $a \\ge 0, b > 0$. Example: $\\sqrt{\\frac{15}{64}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{8}$."
    },
    {
      "front": "Simplify $\\sqrt{108}$.",
      "back": "Factor: $\\sqrt{36 \\cdot 3} = \\sqrt{36} \\cdot \\sqrt{3} = 6\\sqrt{3}$."
    },
    {
      "back": "$$ \\sqrt{9 \\cdot x^2 \\cdot x} = 3x\\sqrt{x} $$",
      "front": "Simplify $\\sqrt{9x^3}$."
    },
    {
      "front": "What does it mean to [[kw:rationalize the denominator]]?",
      "back": "Eliminate a radical from the denominator of a fraction by multiplying numerator and denominator by an appropriate form of 1."
    },
    {
      "front": "Rationalize: $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}$.",
      "back": "Multiply by $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\sqrt{5}}$: $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}$."
    },
    {
      "front": "What are [[kw:conjugates]] in radical expressions?",
      "back": "Binomials $a\\sqrt{b} + c\\sqrt{d}$ and $a\\sqrt{b} - c\\sqrt{d}$. Their product has no radicals: $(a\\sqrt{b})^2 - (c\\sqrt{d})^2 = a^2b - c^2d$."
    },
    {
      "back": "Multiply by $\\frac{2+\\sqrt{3}}{2+\\sqrt{3}}$: $\\frac{7(2+\\sqrt{3})}{4-3} = 14 + 7\\sqrt{3}$.",
      "front": "Simplify $\\frac{7}{2 - \\sqrt{3}}$ using conjugates."
    },
    {
      "front": "What are [[kw:like radicals]]?",
      "back": "Radicals with the same index and radicand. Example: $5\\sqrt{7}$ and $-8\\sqrt{7}$ are like; $\\sqrt{7}$ and $\\sqrt{11}$ are not."
    },
    {
      "back": "Combine like radicals: $(5-8)\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{11} = -3\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{11}$.",
      "front": "Simplify $5\\sqrt{7} + \\sqrt{11} - 8\\sqrt{7}$."
    },
    {
      "back": "Simplify $\\sqrt{20} = 2\\sqrt{5}$. Then $10\\sqrt{5} + 2\\sqrt{5} = 12\\sqrt{5}$.",
      "front": "Simplify $10\\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{20}$."
    },
    {
      "back": "Simplify $\\sqrt{75}=5\\sqrt{3}$. Inside: $\\sqrt{3} - 5\\sqrt{3} = -4\\sqrt{3}$. Multiply: $\\sqrt{5}(-4\\sqrt{3}) = -4\\sqrt{15}$.",
      "front": "Simplify $\\sqrt{5}(\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{75})$."
    },
    {
      "back": "Factor: $\\sqrt[3]{-64 \\cdot 2} = \\sqrt[3]{-64} \\cdot \\sqrt[3]{2} = -4\\sqrt[3]{2}$.",
      "front": "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{-128}$."
    },
    {
      "front": "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{y}{216}}$.",
      "back": "$$ \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{y}}{\\sqrt[3]{216}} = \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{y}}{6} $$"
    },
    {
      "front": "The distance to the horizon is $d = \\sqrt{\\frac{3h}{2}}$. Find $d$ when $h=5$ ft.",
      "back": "$$ \\sqrt{\\frac{15}{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2} \\approx 2.74 \\text{ miles} $$"
    }
  ],
